# .ctsignore — gitignore-syntax paths that `cts-sync.sh update` will never touch.

# Use for: customized CTS files, pruned CTS files (prevents re-adding them),

# and project-only additions placed under payload directories.

# A leading "/" anchors to the project root: "/AGENTS.md" protects only the

# root file; a bare "AGENTS.md" would also match nested files with that name.

# Pruned: project uses Angular only — Vue/React agents+skills removed.

.claude/agents/vue-developer.md
.claude/agents/react-developer.md
.claude/skills/vue-expert/
.claude/skills/react-expert/

# NOTE: Penny's Mongo/Mongoose/Typegoose, onion architecture, LIVR, and other
# per-file customizations now live as override files instead of whole-file
# forks — see AGENTS.local.md and rules/local/{architecture,code-style,
# validation-authorization,dependencies,docker-commands,nx-generators,
# testing,workflow}.md. Those upstream paths are no longer .ctsignore'd and
# receive plain CTS overwrites again, with the overrides layered on top per
# the lex-specialis convention.
#
# rules/architecture-angular.md, rules/architecture-backend.md,
# rules/code-style-angular.md, rules/code-style-backend.md are project-only
# splits that were never CTS payload (not present in claude-ts's
# cts-payload.txt / rules/cts/) — nothing to protect them from, so no entry
# needed here either.

# Public architecture docs — Penny-authored, never regenerated by CTS sync.

/ARCHITECTURE.md
/DECISIONS.md
/CONTEXT.md

